WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.195
Lesson 4.3.

00:00:02.195 --> 00:00:04.970
Liquid staking (LSTs).

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:07.120
By the end of this lesson, you'll be

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:09.793
able to use liquid staking tokens knowing how

00:00:09.793 --> 00:00:12.175
they accrue value and how they can depeg.

00:00:13.475 --> 00:00:14.765
Here's the plan.

00:00:14.765 --> 00:00:16.450
First, the key ideas.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:19.165
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:19.165 --> 00:00:20.690
Then, your checklist.

00:00:20.690 --> 00:00:22.852
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:24.152 --> 00:00:28.779
A liquid staking token (LST) represents staked assets plus

00:00:28.779 --> 00:00:32.922
rewards, and can be traded or used as collateral.

00:00:32.922 --> 00:00:36.021
Value accrues by rebasing (your balance grows)

00:00:36.021 --> 00:00:38.461
or an exchange rate that rises (each

00:00:38.461 --> 00:00:41.332
token is worth more of the underlying).

00:00:41.332 --> 00:00:43.721
In stress, an LST can trade at

00:00:43.721 --> 00:00:46.342
a discount to what it redeems for.

00:00:47.642 --> 00:00:50.157
Let's work an example, step by step.

00:00:50.157 --> 00:00:56.019
An exchange-rate LST goes from 1.000 to 1.030

00:00:56.019 --> 00:01:00.652
of the underlying over a year: 3%.

00:01:00.652 --> 00:01:02.288
In a panic it trades

00:01:02.288 --> 00:01:04.301
at 0.98 on the market.

00:01:04.301 --> 00:01:08.762
Holders who can wait for redemption (queue) recover 1.03;

00:01:08.762 --> 00:01:12.446
holders forced to sell take the 2% discount.

00:01:12.446 --> 00:01:15.019
Never borrow so close to the limit

00:01:15.019 --> 00:01:17.666
that an LST discount liquidates you.

00:01:18.967 --> 00:01:20.427
Here's your checklist.

00:01:20.427 --> 00:01:21.962
Do it now, for real.

00:01:21.962 --> 00:01:25.957
First, Accrual method known (rebase vs exchange rate).

00:01:25.957 --> 00:01:28.792
Next, Redemption path and queue length known.

00:01:28.792 --> 00:01:32.042
And finally, Discount alert set if used as collateral.

00:01:33.342 --> 00:01:34.552
Question 1.

00:01:34.552 --> 00:01:37.432
Two ways LSTs pass on rewards?

00:01:41.852 --> 00:01:45.692
The answer: Rebasing balances, or a rising exchange rate.

00:01:46.992 --> 00:01:48.237
Question 2.

00:01:48.237 --> 00:01:50.472
What is an LST discount?

00:01:54.892 --> 00:01:56.609
The answer: Its market price

00:01:56.609 --> 00:01:58.682
falling below its redemption value.

00:01:59.982 --> 00:02:01.252
Question 3.

00:02:01.252 --> 00:02:02.947
Who is hurt most by a discount?

00:02:07.367 --> 00:02:09.186
The answer: Forced sellers and

00:02:09.186 --> 00:02:11.357
leveraged holders who get liquidated.

00:02:12.657 --> 00:02:15.172
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:02:15.172 --> 00:02:19.047
Next up, Lesson 4.4: Restaking & shared security.
